The 3rd Commandment:


You shall keep holy the Sabbath!


Who takes the trouble to understand a commandment? When you see how children and adults tend to treat the commandments of their God so carelessly, any serious-thinking person could and should be horrified.


The commandments are learned in school and discussed superficially. People are happy when they have absorbed the wording and can give some information about it, as long as there is a danger that they will be asked about it. When they leave school and enter business life, they soon forget the wording and with it the meaning. The best proof that they were not really interested in what their Lord and God required of them.


But he does not even demand anything from this, but in love gives all people what they urgently need! The light noticed how far people were going astray. So God, like an educator, faithfully showed them the way that leads them to eternal existence in the bright kingdom of the spirit, and thus to their happiness, while non-compliance must lead to people's misfortune and ruin!


This is precisely why it is not really correct to speak of commandments . Rather, they are very well-intentioned pieces of advice, showing the right path through materiality, which it has been the desire of human spirits themselves to get to know.


But even this beautiful thought has no effect on man. He is literally too stuck in his own way of thinking and does not want to see or hear anything other than the views he has constructed for himself, which his small earthly knowledge has allowed him to construct.


He does not feel how materiality carries him ever further, ever further, to the limit where for the last time he is faced with either/or, the decision that now remains decisive for his entire being, after which he must follow the path he has chosen to the end, without being able to turn back, even if he finally comes to some realization. Then it comes too late and only serves to increase his torment.


In order to help people to gain insight in time despite their errors , God gave them the third commandment, the advice to keep the holy day holy!


If the commandment had been fulfilled, the longing to strive towards the light would have gradually arisen in every person throughout the ages, and with this longing the path would have been revealed that would have led him to the fulfillment of his wishes, which would increasingly condense into prayer. Then man would be in a different position today! Spiritually permeated, ripe for the kingdom that must now come.


So listen and act, so that the fulfillment of the commandment may prepare your way.


You must keep the holiday holy! You! It is clearly stated in the words that you must consecrate the holiday, make it holy for yourself !


A holiday is a time of celebration, when you rest from the work that your journey on earth imposes on you. But you don't consecrate the time of celebration, the day of rest, if you only want to take care of your body. Nor if you seek distraction through games, drinking or dancing.


The ceremony should lead you to quietly reflect on your thoughts and feelings, to look back on your earthly life to date, especially the past working days of the last week, and to draw useful applications for your future from this. You can always look back on six days, but anything that lasts longer is easily forgotten.


It is inevitable that your feelings will gradually rise and you will become a seeker of the truth. Once you are a real seeker, you will be shown a path. And just as you are only exploring and researching a new path here on earth, which is unknown to you until now, you should also take careful steps on the new spiritual paths that open up to you, step by step, in order to always keep firm ground under your feet. You must not jump, as then there is a greater risk of falling.


By thinking and feeling in this way during the festive hours of your earthly existence, you will never lose anything, but only gain.


No one sanctifies a celebration by going to church if they do not then, during the quiet time, reflect on what they heard there in order to properly absorb it and live by it. The priest cannot sanctify your day if you do not do it yourself. Always consider whether the actual meaning of God's word is in complete harmony with what you are doing. In this way, you will sanctify the holiday; for through peaceful contemplation it has acquired the content for which it was established.


Each holiday becomes a milestone on your path, which retroactively gives the days of your physical activity the value that they should have for the maturation of your soul. They are then not lived in vain, and you are constantly making progress.


To sanctify does not mean to waste. As soon as you neglect this, you miss the time that was allowed for you to mature, and after the world change, which is now slowly closing its rays around you, there is only a short time left to make up for what you have missed, provided that you use all the strength that remains to you.


Therefore, keep the holiday holy! Be it in your home or, better still, in nature, which helps you to become more awake in thought and feeling! In doing so, fulfill the Lord's commandment. It is for your benefit!


